<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Cenbank sells dollars at 1.0485 per dlr.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Cenbank sells dollars at 1.0485 per dlr.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's central bank sold dollars at 1.0485 reais at a dollar tender in the commercial foreign exchange market, dealers said.  </p>
<p>They said the auction's result indicates a change in the real-dollar mini-band to between 1.0435 and 1.0485 per dollar. But the market was still waiting for the Central Bank to confirm the new mini-band because it did not buy dollars at the auction, which is how it normally sets the mini-band.</p>
<p>The previous mini-band was set on Jan 21 between 1.0430 and 1.0480 reais per dollar.</p>
<p>(-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418)</p>
